QuickFIX MinGW-w64 patch for MiniOEMS
=====================================
Upstream: https://github.com/quickfix/quickfix  commit 386ce46e917ae494ab6e90b1be90fd421cdbe3f9
Licence:  QuickFIX Software License, Version 1.0 (BSD-style). This patch modifies QuickFIX source.

Why: QuickFIX detects Windows with _MSC_VER (Microsoft's compiler only). MinGW-w64 targets
Windows with GCC, so it fell through to the POSIX branches (arpa/inet.h, poll.h, fcntl...)
which do not exist on Windows. This patch routes MinGW through QuickFIX's existing Windows
(Winsock / _beginthreadex) code paths:
  - `#ifdef _MSC_VER`  -> `#if defined(_MSC_VER) || defined(__MINGW32__)`  (platform checks)
  - `#ifndef _MSC_VER` -> `#if !defined(_MSC_VER) && !defined(__MINGW32__)`
  - cmake/QuickfixPlatformSettings.cmake: also generate the Allocator.h stub on MinGW
  - src/getopt.c (test runner only): MinGW has no __progname
  - THREAD_PROC uses __stdcall (not _stdcall), which MinGW also accepts in strict -std=c++20 mode
(src/C++/config.h is left alone: QuickFIX regenerates it from cmake_config.h.in on every configure.)
It has no effect on Linux/macOS (GCC/Clang there do not define __MINGW32__).
Verified on Windows 11 + MSYS2 MinGW-w64 GCC 16.1: QuickFIX acceptance tests 467/467 passed.
Apply with: git apply mingw.patch   (git ignores this header)

diff --git a/cmake/QuickfixPlatformSettings.cmake b/cmake/QuickfixPlatformSettings.cmake
index ac54cdd..09cbc5f 100644
--- a/cmake/QuickfixPlatformSettings.cmake
+++ b/cmake/QuickfixPlatformSettings.cmake
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ set( CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS "-m64 -lrt" CACHE STRING "Executable link flags" FOR
 set( CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS "-m64 -lrt" CACHE STRING "shared link flags" FORCE )
 endif()
 
-if(NOT WIN32)
+if(NOT WIN32 OR MINGW)
 find_file (FOUND_ALLOCATOR_HDR NAMES Allocator.h PATHS ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/C++/ NO_DEFAULT_PATH)
 if (NOT FOUND_ALLOCATOR_HDR)
 message("-- Generating empty Allocator.h")
